## 1. Who we are

This Privacy Policy explains how {company} (“{store}”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses and protects your personal data when you use this website and purchase from us. It is published in accordance with the Information Technology Act, 2000, its rules, and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.

## 2. Information we collect

- **Account details** you give us when registering: name, email address, password (stored only in encrypted form by our commerce platform) and, optionally, phone number.
- **Order details**: items purchased, shipping and billing addresses, contact phone number and order history.
- **Payment information**: payments are processed by our payment partners (Stripe, Razorpay and Cashfree). Card and UPI details are entered on their secure forms and are not stored on our servers; we receive only the payment status and a transaction reference.
- **Communications** you send us, for example support emails.
- **Technical data** such as browser type, device information and IP address, which our hosting and commerce infrastructure processes to deliver the site securely.

## 3. Cookies and local storage

We use a small number of essential browser storage items, without which parts of the site would not work:

- a sign-in / cart session token stored in your browser’s local storage, which keeps your cart and account session;
- a currency preference cookie;
- a display preference (grid or list view) on product listings.

Our payment partners may set their own cookies on their checkout forms for fraud prevention. We do not currently use advertising cookies.

## 4. How we use your information

- to create and manage your account;
- to process, deliver and support your orders, including returns and refunds;
- to communicate with you about your orders and respond to your requests;
- to prevent fraud and keep the website secure;
- to comply with legal, tax and accounting obligations.

We process your data on the basis of your consent and for the legitimate purposes of fulfilling your orders and meeting our legal obligations.

## 5. Who we share it with

We do not sell your personal data. We share it only as needed with:

- payment partners (Stripe, Razorpay, Cashfree) to process payments;
- courier and logistics partners to deliver your orders;
- our hosting and e-commerce platform providers, who process data on our behalf;
- authorities, where required by law.

## 6. How long we keep it

We keep account data while your account is active, and order records for as long as required by applicable tax and accounting laws. You can ask us to delete your account at any time (see below).

## 7. Your rights

Subject to applicable law, you may:

- access a summary of the personal data we hold about you;
- correct or update it — most details can be edited directly in your account;
- request erasure of your personal data;
- withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;
- nominate another person to exercise these rights on your behalf;
- raise a grievance with us and, if unresolved, with the Data Protection Board of India.

To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below.

## 8. Security

We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections (HTTPS). No method of transmission over the internet is completely secure, however.

## 9. Children

Our website is intended for adults. Purchases for children must be made by a parent or guardian.

## 10. Changes to this policy

We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date above shows when it last changed.

